  "question": {
    "text": "The volume of a cube is increasing at the rate of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The rate (in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>sec</mi></math>) at which the surface area is increasing when the edge of the cube is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo></math> is"
